TI  - Achieving Environmental sustainability through the adoption of industry 4.0: an exploratory case study within the information technology industry.
AU  - EL MERROUN, Mohamed
AU  - ISTVAN JANOS, Bartók
AU  - ALKHLAIFAT, Osama
PY  - 2024
JO  - Logistics, Supply Chain, Sustainability & Global Challenges
AB  - The article delves into the adoption of Industry 4.0 in the information technology sector, outlining challenges such as decision-making limitations, data underutilization, skill shortages, and integration issues. A prominent company addressed these obstacles through investments in training, data handling, cybersecurity, and IT-OT fusion. It stresses the significance of overcoming these hurdles for successful Industry 4.0 integration and environmental preservation, particularly in waste, CO2 emissions, and energy management. The research underscores the pivotal role of AI in efficiently managing environmental data and promoting sustainable business practices.
