TI  - Generative AI in Cloud CRM: Securing Intelligent Workflows in Multi-Cloud Environments
AU  - Soni, Hemant
AU  - Perla, Srikanth
AU  - Maddela, Srinivas
AU  - Kumar, Uttam
PY  - 2025
JO  - 2025 IEEE 3rd Global Conference on Wireless Computing and Networking (GCWCN), Wireless Computing and Networking (GCWCN), 2025 IEEE 3rd Global Conference on
AB  - The fast adoption of Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) inside Cloud-based Customer Relationship Management (CRM) platforms has completely changed the way the enterprises monitor customer data, automate interactions, and obtain strategic insights. Nonetheless, the implementation of GenAI-based CRM systems into a multi-cloud setup poses complicated issues with data security, model management, and workflow coordination. The paper proposes a cohesive structure of Securing Intelligent Workflows in Multi-Cloud CRM Environments based on a hybrid architecture which is a combination of Generative AI, federated policy enforcement and adaptive data pipelines. The system proposed automates decision-making and content creation as well as customer interaction via heterogeneous clouds like AWS, Azure, and GCP, based on large language models (LLMs), and meets the security requirements of systems like GDPR and ISO/IEC 27001. An AI-supported and zero-trust security model can improve the ability to resist insider threats and attempts at data exfiltration. The results of the experiment prove the better workflow efficiency, decreased policy violation rate, and higher accuracy of automation in comparison to the traditional CRM automation systems. Cross-cloud scalability, secure API orchestration, and explainable AI-driven audit trails have also been identified in the paper as enablers of trustful and intelligent CRM automation in enterprise ecosystems.
